hello and welcome to Playstation grenade  anthem first grabbed our attention at e3  last year but surprisingly fell silent  shortly after now one year later details  are finally here to add a little more  context to anthem so much so that we  have a release date February 22nd of  2019 so here's everything we learned  about anthem at e3 2018 I'd love to talk  about the javelin suit right away but  first let's figure out where we start  the game the world of anthem is  deliberately unfinished and ambiguous  the gods that created this world known  as shapers used a powerful piece of  technology known as the anthem of  creation to form each element of the  planet for an unbeknownst reason those  gods left the planet half complete but  the tools they created the world with  still remain scattered throughout the  world with all that godlike tech laying  around it's only a question of when  someone will attempt to use it for evil  so that's where we step in we play as  the freelancers a specially trained  group of operatives who are capable of  piloting a javelin  a futuristic excel suit which looks to  be ironmans wet dream the javelins are  characterized by four subsets Ranger  Colossus interceptor and storm the devs  have shed a little light on the classes  starting with the Ranger which is a  general suit which is balanced and  thrives on up close and personal combat  the Colossus on the other hand is  described as a specialized unit  utilizing heavy artillery we've seen him  wielding a mortar and a flamethrower  the Colossus who is quickly becoming my  personal favorite was also shown  charging through mines with his shield  for cover we didn't hear much about the  Interceptor class or storm for that  matter but we can see by the demo  footage the Interceptor looks to be more  agile and the storm class uses elemental  powers we could apply traditional MMO  and RPG roles to the javelins with the  range of being the DPS the Colossus  could be the tank the storm could be a  mage and at a push the Interceptor is a  healer maybe not let's leave that on the  Shelf until we see their skill sets in  future reveals the devs have also noted  that each chaplain class was based on  the elements a major point to be stated  is that you play as a pilot not a  javelin therefore you can pick and  choose which exosuit you want to take on  each mission you and your chosen squads  will need to balance the weapons the  items and the javelins you choose to  complement one another especially in  difficult endgame activities but on the  other hand you could jump in alone after  a hard day grab the Colossus and destroy  everything in your path the choice is  yours we also know that each javelin  class has unique skills melee attacks  defensive setups and good old Ultimates  to use when more info is released I'll  be back to break down each Javelin class  especially the storm so that leads us  onto the enemies in anthem the native  wildlife always possesses a potential  risk but who will be the main villain of  the  in terms of the narrative-driven enemy  your fall will be the Dominion these  folks are aggressive wicked and  malicious and they're attempting to  harness the power of the gods  aka the anthem of creation to build  super weapons designed to bring down  your javelin and anything else you love  too and on top of that unconfirmed alien  invaders known as scars are here to keep  both sides on their toes in a constant  three-way power struggle anthem is  trying to give us questions we want to  find answers to we've been told that the  story is solo driven but it's also a  fully-fledged shared world so you'll  need up to three friends to be with you  every endeavor and mission any destiny  players in the house remember the first  time you've finished a raid and the  awesome memories that invokes well  that's what anthem wants but with all  aspects of the game immersive and  emergent gameplay they call it although  this is very much a shared world shooter  there is one place you cannot take your  friends with you your home hub of fort  Asus locked behind a massive wall to  keep out the enemy you'll return here  often to hand in quests and to chat with  the occasional NPC or two this will act  as your campaign home which is solely  for you to signify this change the  camera will switch to first-person  whenever you go back home so  third-person for the shared world  first-person for when you're back at fob  Tarsus so why would fort Asus be a  private experience it's pretty simple by  making this zone a solitary place anthem  can make changes to your private world  that reflects where you are in the  game's narrative maybe for Tarsus was  invaded and buildings were demolished  you'd see that devastation when  returning home whereas your mate Dave  may not be that far in the story and we  wouldn't ruin it for him I'm curious to  know your opinion on our private refuge  we call for Tarsus do you want to share  your home base I'll keep the narrative  changes to yourself there are many RPG  elements at work in anthem both centered  around your pilots and each respective  javelin for example investing in your  pilot's with an ability such as jumping  higher with jets this will be given to  all your javelins whereas any upgrades  to your traveling specifically remain on  that single javelin let's take this  point further and look at customization  in anthem the first way you'll stand out  from your friends on the battlefield is  the two weapons you choose to bring  along although we haven't seen the full  range of weapons available yet we know  that anthem will use weapon rarities to  signify the epicness of each firearm and  collectible in last year's demo the  Ranger picked up Yara's wrath the  legendary vault rifle showing us that  weapons do indeed have levels applied  and have stats broken down into damage  accuracy range rate of fire and ammo  capacity here's something I found quite  interesting whilst on a mission with a  light javelin such as the interceptor or  storm you may find a weapon which can  only be used with a heavier frame ie the  Ranger or the super-heavy Colossus  forcing you to change your character and  play style to utilize that new weapon in  addition to this along with the weapons  you choose you have two extra slots for  tools such as energy explosives or good  old grenades to name a few  in terms of aesthetic customization  anthem is all about expression we're  talking complete paint jobs only a small  portion were shown but that included a  Mass Effect Easter Egg and this paint  job which I'll be forcing all my clan to  wear customization and monetization come  hand-in-hand these days which were also  addressed by the devs loot boxes will  not exist in anthem but purchasable  items will but they won't offer any  gameplay advantages it's all about  cosmetics only if you haven't guessed  already anthem is intended to be played  for years it's an ongoing service which  promises to dynamically change and  evolve during its lifespan will be  grinding through missions to find the  perfect weapon upgrading our characters  and equipment will be building  relationships with NPCs and more  importantly other players in the world  will be fighting enemies with super  weapons and attempting to save humanity  we'll be living every moment which we  are told is filled with deep exploration  and law for months and years of  I can't say if anthem will be a great  game but I can say it has a great deal  of potential what do you guys think  anthem releases on February 22nd 2019 on  ps4 Xbox and PC I'm Adam from  PlayStation granade it's been a pleasure  I'll see you next time  you
 

